# Local changes to sequential-storage 8.0.0, confined to src/map.rs.
# The root, fuzz and emulator workspaces all use this exact vendored file.
#
# 1. Warm key pointers only after a complete scan; propagate read refusals.
# 2. Retire oldest records first so interrupted remove cannot resurrect old data.
# 3. Bound key decoding by each item's declared length, including cached hits.
# 4. Reserve an exact erased candidate span before an authenticated intent,
#    then append/read/discard that span without allocating or repairing it.
# 5. Expose unrepaired lookup and raw full-value matching. Readers authenticate
#    expected payloads; mutation requires mapped-value validation before GC.
# 6. Validate post-repair owners before GC and propagate all read refusals.
#
# Regenerate against pristine crates.io 8.0.0 src/map.rs; preserve CRLF.

